/-!
# The scalar–scalar `++` harmonic response from the corpus Green function

With the forcing `ssForcing = −(r²(r²−1)/4)·ssMasterSource` transported to the horizon coordinate
`z = 1 − r⁻²` (`rOfZ z = √((1−z)⁻¹)`), the corpus regular-horizon/normalizable-AdS Green response at
overtone `n` and angular parameter `chi`, pulled back to the exterior radius, solves the undressed
sourced master equation of the scalar–scalar source (`greenSS_masterEquation`) and is smooth on the
exterior by bootstrapping the hypergeometric equation (`greenSS_contDiffOn`). Consequently the
reconstructed Kodama–Ishibashi radial functions built from it satisfy all seven sourced harmonic
Einstein equations at every exterior radius (`greenSS_equation_TT`, …): this is the per-harmonic
`++` scalar–scalar response at the fundamental's harmonic, with the causal boundary conditions of the
corpus Green function.
-/

set_option linter.unusedVariables false

